  clock: 5  # 20e3
  nonce: '20e3'  # 20e3
  message: "SATISFIED. The item's statement is the catalogue tag -- 'a call that can only read stdin must carry a boundary AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP maps to untrusted_input' -- and all 16 rows across go/python/c/haskell/scala now carry ipc_recv (verified live: load_catalog(lang).lookup_with_module returns ipc_recv for fmt.Scan, builtins.input, stdio.scanf/getchar, Prelude.getLine, scala.io.StdIn.readLine).\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, re-running the item's own repro and closing the gap it recorded as DEAD. When this shipped (08-30) python input() emitted no call edge (INV-foluz) so the row was present-and-dead. Phase A (INV-foluz, merged) fixed the bare-Name emission. NOW LIVE, measured just now:\n  prog.py: buf = input(); subprocess.run(buf, shell=True)\n  verify-claims -> violated: 'builtins.input [python:prog.py:2-4:handler] -> subprocess.run' [origins: 1 ipc_recv], confidence precise.\nc and go were confirmed live in this item's 08-30 discussion (scanf/getchar/fmt.Scan all FIRE -> ipc_recv). So 3 of 5 languages reach the corrected rows; the canonical scanf-then-system / input-then-run flow is now detectable where it was silent.\n\nTHE TWO REMAINING ARMS ARE SEPARATE ANALYZER DEFECTS, filed not folded (the item's own instruction -- 'pinning the three dead ones would pin a bug in place'):\n  haskell  no call edge for 's <- getLine' in a do-block bind = WI-manir (zero-arg IO actions in infix/bind positions).\n  scala    scala.io.StdIn.readLine emitted hint-less + ambiguous, withheld by design = INV-vokut (filed now, INV-linub's receiver-typing class for scala).\nNeither is a catalogue defect; both become useful the day their analyzer emits a resolvable edge. The catalogue -- this item's subject -- is correct and reachable."  # 20e3
